meta {
  name: verify email (dj-rest-auth)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/rest-auth/registration/account-confirm-email/
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    // Confirmation key from the emailed link.
    "key": "PASTE_KEY_FROM_THE_EMAIL_LINK"
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  **Use `POST /student/registration/verify-email/` instead.**

  dj-rest-auth's own confirmation view. It marks the address verified but returns
  only `{"detail": "ok"}` -- no tokens, so the user still has to log in
  afterwards. Ours confirms and logs them in in one step.

  Kept because allauth reverses this route's name
  (`account_email_verification_sent`) in parts of its flow.

  ## API example response
  {
    "detail": "ok"
  }
}
